error[ffi_not_constant]: `fixedbugs-2116-calls.h` has `R_CNT`, but not as a constant — clang cannot read its value while compiling
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2116-a-record-constant-whose-value-is-no-constant-is-refused.hero:25:5
     |
  25 |     constant R_CNT: pt  #~ ffi_not_constant
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: a `constant` names one value forever (§4.4), and clang reads `R_CNT` as something computed each time it is read, an object, a call or a statement expression it does not fold, so nothing holds two reads of it to one answer: the mutable global §4.2 forbids. A value computed in C is reached through a function of the program's own that returns it, written in a header beside this file and bound by `extern` naming that header like any function: `static inline <its C type> hero_R_CNT(void) { <its C type> value = R_CNT; return value; }`

